{
  "summary": "Updates the Guix time-machine pinned commit to a newer upstream revision and adjusts build manifests for updated package recipes. It switches the build environment to CMake 4.3.3 with CMAKE_LINK_WARNING_AS_ERROR, drops a custom osslsigncode definition in favor of upstream Guix, updates python-lief to 1.0.0, and disables fixincludes on gcc-sans-libc.",
  "problem": "The pinned Guix build environment lacks newer toolchains such as GCC 16 and Clang 22/23, relies on an out-of-date CMake version, triggers deprecation warnings on package module imports, and requires an in-tree package override for osslsigncode that upstream Guix now provides natively.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description highlights upstream toolchain upgrades: \"cmake `3.31.10` -> `4.3.3`\", \"Default Clang/LLVM updated to `22.x` and `23.x` available\", \"GCC 16 now available\", and \"python-lief `0.17.6` -> `1.0.0`\".",
    "Commit 1fdb268244 addresses an upstream deprecation warning: \"manifest_build.scm:279:8: warning: 'ninja' is deprecated, use '(@ (gnu packages build-tools) ninja)' instead\"."
  ],
